index 0000000..7dd4f76
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/privacy-audit.md
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# Privacy audit
+
+Scope: sign-in/sign-up, shared layout, document metadata and response headers.
+
+## Changes
+
+- Account forms collect only username and password. A shared notice explains the demo, discourages real or reused credentials, names the external recipient and purpose, and links to the privacy policy.
+- Authentication POSTs omit cookies and referrers, bypass browser caches, and reject redirects. Responses are not parsed or persisted; raw backend errors are not displayed. Passwords are cleared on success and failure. Autocomplete supports password managers; registration enforces its displayed minimum requirements.
+- Submit buttons remain disabled until hydration attaches the handler, avoiding native form submission to page routes. Both forms mark themselves as excluded from tracking, although no tracking script is loaded.
+- Removed layout analytics, dormant ad-script markup, the fireplace ad integration, Google Fonts and preconnects. Text uses the existing serif fallback. The footer privacy link now has a working destination.
+- Documents use UTF-8 and a no-referrer meta policy. Middleware also sets Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy, X-Content-Type-Options and Cache-Control: no-store for dynamic responses.
+- Removed automatic session initialization on page views. Existing reading-list writes create sessions on demand.
+- Replaced generic policy boilerplate with the actual data flow and explicit limits of what this repository establishes.
+
+## Remaining boundaries
+
+- Authentication and hosting infrastructure are outside this repository. Password handling, logging, retention, deletion and a real privacy contact need verification before using real account data. Client-side changes cannot establish these guarantees.
+- External article images still contact their hosts; document referrers are suppressed. Article ad placeholders remain inert without the removed ad client.
+- Diagnostic article code, including the plant-stats cookie-size demonstration, remains outside this audit's implementation scope and is disclosed in the policy. It should be reviewed before a production launch.
+- Middleware applies to application responses, not static files served directly by a CDN or reverse proxy. Deployment-level header configuration needs separate verification.
+
+Validation: `pnpm run build` passed. Ten automated source-level checks passed using mocked requests and React hooks: both forms across success, rejection and network failure; disabled submit before hydration; middleware headers and no session initialization; and layout metadata with no third-party analytics/font requests. `git diff --check` passed. The build reported Vite plugin deprecation and dynamic-route getStaticPaths warnings. No browser verification, dev/preview server, deployed authentication call or generated server-entrypoint import was performed.
