-    <h2>1. An overview of data protection</h2>
-    <p><strong>General information</strong></p>
-    <p>The following information will provide you with an easy to navigate overview of what will happen with your personal data when you visit our website. The term “personal data” comprises all data that can be used to personally identify you. For detailed information about the subject matter of data protection, please consult our Data Protection Declaration, which we have included beneath this copy.</p>
-    
-    <h2>2. General information and mandatory information</h2>
-    <p><strong>Data protection</strong></p>
-    <p>The operators of this website and its pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously. Hence, we handle your personal data as confidential information and in compliance with the statutory data protection regulations and this Data Protection Declaration.</p>
-    <p>Whenever you use this website, a variety of personal information will be collected. Personal data comprises data that can be used to personally identify you. This Data Protection Declaration explains which data we collect as well as the purposes we use this data for. It also explains how, and for which purpose the information is collected.</p>
-    
-    <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <p>The DevTools Times is a demonstration website. You can read articles without creating an account. This notice describes data handling in this website's code; it does not make promises about services operated outside this repository.</p>
+
+    <h2 id="accounts">Sign-in and sign-up</h2>
+    <p>These forms ask only for a username and password to process a sign-in or registration request. No email address, real name, or profile information is required. Use a made-up username and a password you do not use elsewhere.</p>
+    <p>Only when you submit a form, these two fields are sent over HTTPS to the authentication service at <code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net</code>, using its <code>/times_cdn/api/login</code> or <code>/times_cdn/api/register</code> endpoint. That service also receives connection information such as your IP address. The request omits cookies and the page's referrer.</p>
+    <p>The page does not log credentials or save credentials or returned tokens in local storage, session storage, or cookies. Passwords are cleared from the form after each request. Your browser or password manager may offer to save them according to your settings. A successful sign-in in this demo does not create a persistent signed-in session.</p>
+    <p>The authentication service is maintained outside this repository. Its password storage, logging, retention periods, and account deletion process have not been verified here. Do not submit sensitive or reused credentials. A production service needs verified retention and deletion details and a working privacy contact before collecting real account information.</p>
+
+    <h2 id="tracking">Analytics, advertising, and external resources</h2>
+    <p>The shared page layout does not load third-party analytics, advertising scripts, or remotely hosted fonts. There is no analytics or advertising preference to enable on this site.</p>
+    <p>Some articles and teasers load images from external hosts, including Imgur and the CinemAI demo service. Those hosts receive connection information when images load. Pages use a no-referrer policy so these requests do not include the page URL. Following an external link takes you to that site's own data practices.</p>
+
+    <h2>Reading lists and cookies</h2>
+    <p>Changing your reading list stores article identifiers in a server-side session associated with a session cookie. This supports saving and removing articles. Browsing alone does not initialize a reading-list session. You can remove saved articles through the reading list and clear the site's cookies in your browser to disconnect that browser from its session. Clearing cookies does not itself delete the server-side record; session expiry and cleanup depend on the hosting configuration.</p>
+    <p>Some demo articles include diagnostic requests. The “Silent Architects” article contains a cookie-size demonstration that sets test cookies scoped to its plant-stats API path. These are separate from account information and can also be removed through browser settings.</p>
+
+    <h2>Hosting and questions</h2>
+    <p>The website host receives the connection information needed to serve requests and may keep operational logs. Hosting log retention and authentication-service retention cannot be determined from this website's code. The <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}legal/imprint`}>imprint</a> identifies this project as a demo; it currently does not provide a verified privacy contact or an account deletion mechanism.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
